    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0194" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/841b: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d108-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-12-03T18:00:00-05:00">December 3, 1936—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President ratified the London Naval Treaty, 1936, on May 28. So far no other
                    Government has ratified although the Treaty was drafted to come into effect on
                    January 1, 1937. Any information which may come to you with regard to the
                    intentions of the Government to which you are accredited in respect of
                    ratification of the Treaty should be promptly reported.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d108-f1" n="20" type="source" xml:id="d108-f1-content">
                <p>The same telegram was sent to the Embassies in France and Italy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
